# Navigation via Coordinator

**Rule:** Screen navigation is declared in **one place** —
`lib/core/coordinator/coordinator.dart`. `Navigator.` and `MaterialPageRoute`
may appear **only** inside `lib/core/coordinator/`. Features, pages and widgets
must express intent by calling a `Coordinator` method, never by constructing
routes or calling `Navigator` directly.

### Why
- One source of truth for routes and transitions.
- Features don't depend on routing mechanics — they just say "go here".
- Migrating to a router (e.g. `go_router`) touches only the Coordinator; every
  call site stays unchanged.

### How it works
`Coordinator` exposes intent-named static methods that take a `BuildContext`:

```dart
abstract final class Coordinator {
  static Future<void> openDevTools(BuildContext context) =>
      _push(context, (_) => const DevToolsGalleryPage());

  static void pop<T>(BuildContext context, [T? result]) =>
      Navigator.of(context).pop(result);

  static Future<T?> _push<T>(BuildContext context, WidgetBuilder builder) =>
      Navigator.of(context).push<T>(MaterialPageRoute<T>(builder: builder));
}
```

### ✅ Good — feature calls the Coordinator
```dart
// in a page/widget
onTap: () => Coordinator.openDevTools(context),
onPressed: () => Coordinator.pop(context),
```

### ❌ Bad — navigation declared inside a feature
```dart
// in a page/widget — NOT allowed
Navigator.of(context).push(
  MaterialPageRoute(builder: (_) => const DevToolsGalleryPage()),
);
Navigator.pop(context);
```

### Notes
- Add a new destination by adding a method to `Coordinator` (and importing the
  target page there) — do not push it from the feature.
- Flutter overlay helpers (`showDialog`, `showModalBottomSheet`,
  `Scaffold.of(context).openDrawer()`) are allowed in widgets since they are not
  `Navigator` calls, but **dismiss them with `Coordinator.pop(context)`**.
